  "releaseNotes": "0.6.0-preview.4: Fail-closed EF Core multitenancy building block. Persistence.EfCore adds the Multitenancy namespace (ITenantScopedEntity, ITenantContextProvider, TenantSaveChangesInterceptor that stamps the resolved tenant and throws MissingTenantContextException/CrossTenantWriteException on missing or cross-tenant writes, UseArhamTenantEnforcement, modelBuilder.UseArhamMultitenancy conventions). Persistence.EfCore.PostgreSql adds TenantSessionConnectionInterceptor (session GUC via parameterized set_config on every connection open — pooling-safe, empty when unresolved), EnableArhamTenantRowLevelSecurity/DisableArhamTenantRowLevelSecurity migration helpers emitting FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY with a fail-closed NULLIF policy, and UseArhamPostgreSqlMultitenancy wiring both interceptors. Includes an env-gated end-to-end RLS proof against real PostgreSQL (non-superuser role enforced). See CHANGELOG.md and docs/Multitenancy.md.",
